# W44-58: libjxl debug-build per-position cost-input dump
#
# Follow-on to f_d_residual_exhausted_2026-05-18 memo "DO consider" #3.
# Closes the W44-21 honest-stop on lack of libjxl-side comparison data.
#
# Date: 2026-05-19
# Workspaces (sibling, mandatory):
#   - jxl-encoder:  ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-58-libjxl-debug-dump
#   - libjxl:       ~/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl--w44-58-debug-dump (git worktree)
#
# Method:
#   1. Patched libjxl `EstimateEntropy` (lib/jxl/enc_ac_strategy.cc:364) to dump
#      per-call cost inputs (strategy, x, y, entropy_mul, covered_blocks,
#      quant_norm16, cmap_x/b, mask1x1_mean_y, entropy_pre_loss, loss_scalar,
#      info_loss_mul, cost_delta, zeros_mul, final_entropy) to a TSV file path
#      from env var `JXL_DUMP_COST_INPUTS_PATH`.
#      VERIFIED bit-identical bitstream when env var unset (MD5 match).
#   2. Patched our `estimate_entropy_full_impl` (jxl-encoder/src/vardct/ac_strategy.rs
#      line ~1228) with the same dump format. VERIFIED bit-identical when env unset.
#   3. Ran cjxl + cjxl-rs on 3 F-D wedge images at d=5 and d=6 (6 cells total).
#   4. Diffed per-(strategy, x, y) shared keys. Source dumps archived at:
#      /mnt/v/output/jxl-encoder/w44-58-libjxl-cost-input-dump/ (~70MB total)
#
# Test images: CID22 1531677, 1418519, 1420710 at d=5,6 e7
# All bitstreams produced with --num_threads 1 (libjxl) and default (ours).
#
# Key findings (see benchmarks/w44_58_diff_*_summary_2026-05-19.txt):
#
#   Fields CONFIRMED bit-exact (median 0, 100% zero):
#     - info_loss_mul, cost_delta, zeros_mul, cmap_x
#
#   Fields with significant divergence (cross-image median abs rel diff):
#     - loss_scalar:       11.6%  (DOMINANT divergence)
#     - final_entropy:      5.6%
#     - entropy_pre_loss:   5.6%
#     - entropy_mul:        1.4%
#     - cmap_b:             0.4%
#
#   Stratified by strategy (shared-key, same entropy_mul, same covered_blocks):
#     DCT8 / DCT32x16 / DCT16x32 / DCT16x16 / DCT32x32:
#       median <0.0002 (essentially bit-exact), p95 <1%
#     AFV0 / AFV1:
#       median 12.4%–12.9% loss_scalar
#       median 5.5%–5.7% entropy_pre_loss
#       p95 32%–35% loss_scalar
#
#   Coverage: only ~31,500 of ~47,700 (strategy,x,y) keys shared between
#   ours and libjxl on each image. We and libjxl explore DIFFERENT strategies
#   at the same positions — the search trees themselves diverge.
#   Strategy-count divergence vs libjxl on 1531677 d=6:
#     strat 4 (DCT16x16): ours 256 calls, libjxl 1024 (×4)
#     strat 5 (DCT32x32): ours 4096 calls, libjxl  268 (we evaluate 15× more)
#     strat 16/17 (AFV2/3): ours 64/128, libjxl 4096/4096 (libjxl evaluates ×30+)
#
# Root cause: AFV (adaptive-frequency-variable, corner DCT) transform pipeline
# is the dominant pure-numerical divergence. Direction is roughly symmetric
# (50/50 positive/negative deltas) but magnitude is large — would explain
# why W44-19's per-block bisection found 264-346 strategy disagreements
# concentrated in the AFV/sub-block-merge regime.
#
# Recommended attack chunk:
#   Audit AFV pipeline end-to-end vs libjxl:
#     - `vardct/afv.rs::afv_transform_from_pixels` (forward; ~lines 194-262)
#     - `vardct/afv.rs::inverse_afv_transform`     (inverse; ~lines 282-362)
#     - `vardct/afv.rs::afv_dct_4x4` / `afv_idct_4x4` (inner 4x4 corner DCT)
#     - `vardct/quant.rs::generate_afv_weights`    (quant weights; verify
#        post-Feb-15 sub-weight row indexing fix is still correct)
#   Compare with libjxl `enc_transforms-inl.h:407 AFVTransformFromPixels` and
#   `dec_transforms-inl.h:400 AFVTransformToPixels`.
#
#   Specific attack: instrument AFV inner-DCT input/output values for a SINGLE
#   block (e.g. 1531677 d=6 strategy=14 x=64 y=64) on BOTH sides — compare
#   the 16 AFV4x4 output coefficients, 16 DCT4x4 outputs, 32 DCT4x8 outputs
#   value-by-value. The dump infra here gives us the post-aggregate values;
#   to isolate which inner stage diverges we need per-coefficient dumps.
#
# Filed issue: imazen/jxl-encoder#XX (see commit message)
